{"embed.js validates message origins using a substring check (discourseUrl.indexOf(e.origin)) which is not a robust origin comparison and can allow spoofed resize messages": 0.8941867351531982, "The embed iframe posts messages using request.referer as targetOrigin which is typically a full URL (includes path/query) and is not a valid origin, so postMessage can throw and resizing can fail": 0.9696425199508667, "Imported content is created with cook_method: raw_html and Post#cook returns raw content unchanged, bypassing PrettyText sanitization, enabling stored XSS from RSS/remote imports": 0.9966097474098206, "app/views/embed/best.html.erb contains invalid ERB syntax (<%- end if %>) which will raise a template compilation error and break /embed/best rendering": 0.9521692395210266, "PollFeed calls i.content.scrub without guarding nil, which can raise NoMethodError and abort the job": 0.9614404439926147, "An unescaped request header (request.referer) is interpolated into JavaScript without JS-escaping": 0.9787095785140991, "embed.js assumes #discourse-comments exists and will throw if missing": 0.6294592022895813, "PollFeed has retry: false so transient feed format issues can permanently prevent imports until the next run": 0.3229218125343323, "TopicEmbed.import_remote fetches remote content via open(url).read without explicit open-uri require, timeouts, or error handling": 0.9030085206031799, "TopicRetriever runs Jobs::PollFeed.new.execute({}) inline for every retrieval attempt when feed polling is enabled, defeating the hourly schedule and causing repeated expensive feed downloads": 0.9471374750137329, "An existing migration (CreateTopTopics) was modified to use force: true which can drop tables if the migration is re-run, risking data loss": 0.8836408853530884}